          "collection_date": "2025-01-08",
          "description": {
            "comment": "The featherfin pearlfish (Ophthalmolebias constanciae) is a species of killifish from the family Rivulidae that is endemic to Brazil. It is restricted to temporary freshwater habitats (like ponds) in the Sao Joao basin in Rio de Janeiro, while all other species in the genus are from Bahia (from Wikipedia entry). This sample was collected from a male adult bred in captivity at Western Michigan University in Kalamazoo, Michigan by Andrew W. Thompson to generate a high-quality reference genome for a study on killifish genomics and the Vertebrate Genomes Project (VGP). Sequencing and genome assembly were conducted at the Vertebrate Genome Lab (VGL) at the Rockefeller University, led by Erich D. Jarvis, Giulio Formenti, and Jennifer Balacco. Manual curation was done by Genoscope in France.",
